<?xml version="1.0" encoding="UTF-8" standalone="no" ?>
<FinalDraft DocumentType="Script" Template="No" Version="5">
<Content>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>EXT. THE MAGNOLIA - REAR DOOR - NIGHT</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Late. The lot is nearly empty. The rear door stands propped open on a brick, kitchen light across the pavement.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>MERLE COBB, 60s, owner of the Magnolia, reading glasses pushed up in his hair, on the phone beside the door. A hardware-store bag at his feet.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>COBB</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Parenthetical"><Text>(into phone)</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>-- no, bring it in the back. The back. ... Monday. Monday&#x27;s fine. ... I said it&#x27;s fine. Tell Dunphy.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He hangs up.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>BIG PETE TILLMAN, 50s, six-four, heavy through the chest and belly, thick hands, comes out the propped door onto the step on his round, and stops when he sees Cobb.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>COBB</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>You hear what&#x27;s going on in town?</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>BIG PETE</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>June?</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>COBB</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>No. Somebody&#x27;s burning buildings.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>He picks up the bag and hands it to Pete.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>COBB</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Nobody comes through my back door.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Cobb goes in. Pete follows him.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Scene Heading"><Text>INT. THE MAGNOLIA - REAR HALL - CONTINUOUS</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Cobb kicks the brick out and lets the door swing shut behind them. Latched. The push bar across it at waist height.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Pete takes a length of chain and a padlock out of the bag, the price sticker still on it. He looks at the door. Then at the push bar.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>BIG PETE</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>That&#x27;s an exit, Merle.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>COBB</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>It&#x27;s a service door. Ain&#x27;t nobody using that at night.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>BIG PETE</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>It&#x27;s got a bar on it.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Cobb says nothing.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Pete holds up the chain.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>BIG PETE</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Are we even allowed? I don&#x27;t think we can chain that door.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>COBB</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>I ain&#x27;t risking somebody walking in here and burning this place down in the middle of the night.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>From the barroom, down the hall, a burst of laughter. Music underneath it. Pete looks that way.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>BIG PETE</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Every night?</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Character"><Text>COBB</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Dialogue"><Text>Every night. Once the kitchen&#x27;s closed.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Pete runs the chain through the push bar and the door frame and snugs it tight. He closes the padlock.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>SNAP.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Cobb takes the key and threads it onto his key ring. Pete glances at the chained door.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Music, voices and bottles clinking come down the hall.</Text></Paragraph>
<Paragraph Type="Action"><Text>Cobb pockets the key ring.</Text></Paragraph>
</Content>
</FinalDraft>
